WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:01.390
OK.

00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:08.019
There is a disturbing new piece in The Atlantic
by Barton Gellman called The Election that

00:00:08.019 --> 00:00:09.830
could break America.

00:00:09.830 --> 00:00:11.270
This is red alert stuff.

00:00:11.270 --> 00:00:12.760
This is not a rehearsal.

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:13.830
Okay.

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:22.560
This piece explains the plan that the Trump
campaign has put together to bypass election

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:23.710
results.

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:30.400
If Donald Trump loses, they have a plan for
how to subvert the election results.

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:35.940
If Joe Biden were to win and if we merely
ignore it, we're not going to be prepared.

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:38.440
So this is really the stuff of nightmares.

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:41.059
Now, I mean, explain the idea to you.

00:00:41.059 --> 00:00:43.469
The idea is the following.

00:00:43.469 --> 00:00:50.950
Trump choosing electors in battleground states,
regardless of who wins the states so that

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:55.410
they will vote for Donald Trump at the electors
convention.

00:00:55.410 --> 00:01:00.359
OK, this is based on what some call a technicality.

00:01:00.359 --> 00:01:06.750
Normally, the popular vote in a state determines
which electors go to D.C. to cast their ballots.

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:12.830
So if Joe Biden wins, Michigan, preselected
Democratic electors go to D.C. and they say

00:01:12.830 --> 00:01:16.159
Michigan pledges our electoral votes for Joe
Biden.

00:01:16.159 --> 00:01:22.930
The idea here is even if Biden wins Michigan,
some Republican strategists and lawyers are

00:01:22.930 --> 00:01:30.170
saying even if Biden wins Michigan, Donald
Trump could say there was fraud in Michigan.

00:01:30.170 --> 00:01:34.720
We are going to send the Republican electors
to D.C. instead of the Democratic electors,

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:39.730
even though supposedly Biden won Michigan,
because I believe that there was fraud.

00:01:39.730 --> 00:01:40.730
That's the idea.

00:01:40.730 --> 00:01:45.970
Now, the immediate reaction from a normal
person would be how the hell do you justify

00:01:45.970 --> 00:01:46.970
it?

00:01:46.970 --> 00:01:48.750
And indeed, the justification is fraud.

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:50.970
Their explanation would be, we believe.

00:01:50.970 --> 00:01:52.450
There was broke voter fraud.

00:01:52.450 --> 00:01:57.390
We don't really believe Biden won Michigan
as an example.

00:01:57.390 --> 00:02:01.380
So because Trump actually won.

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:07.079
Trump is going to select Republican electors
to go to D.C. and represent Michigan.

00:02:07.079 --> 00:02:12.670
The Atlantic explains that, quote, Trump would
ask state legislators to set aside the popular

00:02:12.670 --> 00:02:16.730
vote and exercise their power to choose a
slate of electors directly.

00:02:16.730 --> 00:02:21.300
The longer Trump succeeds in keeping the vote
count in doubt, the more pressure legislators

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:26.209
will feel to act before the safe harbor deadline
expires.

00:02:26.209 --> 00:02:31.830
A Trump campaign legal adviser spoke to the
Atlantic for this story and said that the

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:39.400
goal would be for state legislatures to say
we've been given this constitutional power.

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:43.060
If they don't think the results of their state
are accurate or if they're willing to at least

00:02:43.060 --> 00:02:50.801
suspend disbelief in order to help Trump,
they could say we are overriding the elector

00:02:50.801 --> 00:02:54.130
choices and we're sending Republican electors
to Washington, D.C..

00:02:54.130 --> 00:03:00.930
The chair of the Pennsylvania Republican Party,
Lawrence Tabby's, also spoke to the Atlantic

00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:06.170
and said, quote, I've mentioned it to them
and I hope they're thinking about it, too.

00:03:06.170 --> 00:03:11.930
Referring to this strategy, they are looking
at these strategies.

00:03:11.930 --> 00:03:14.049
This is just one idea we've talked.

00:03:14.049 --> 00:03:20.269
You know, the more pedestrian and obvious
ideas are having an army of lawyers descend

00:03:20.269 --> 00:03:22.310
on states at midnight on November 3rd.

00:03:22.310 --> 00:03:26.770
Well, technically, it would be midnight, November
4th at the end of Election Day.

00:03:26.770 --> 00:03:33.129
And the idea of the Red Mirage scenario would
be because of early in-person voting by Trump

00:03:33.129 --> 00:03:36.530
voters at midnight at the end of Election
Day.

00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:38.930
Trump might have a slight lead in some states.

00:03:38.930 --> 00:03:43.650
However, if all the absentee ballots were
to be counted, those leads might evaporate

00:03:43.650 --> 00:03:44.860
in favor of Joe Biden.

00:03:44.860 --> 00:03:49.569
The idea would be you have lawyers descend
on states at midnight to say stop counting

00:03:49.569 --> 00:03:54.420
absentee ballots, making different legal arguments
in different states.

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:56.100
So this is not a joke.

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:57.269
They are prepared.

00:03:57.269 --> 00:03:58.580
I've said it before.

00:03:58.580 --> 00:04:02.829
If Trump loses, I do believe he will eventually
leave.

00:04:02.829 --> 00:04:08.590
But here are ways he can try to claim he didn't
actually lose either by preventing votes from

00:04:08.590 --> 00:04:09.870
being counted.

00:04:09.870 --> 00:04:12.970
Claiming he won and sending in different electors.

00:04:12.970 --> 00:04:17.510
Trump's legal teams are laying the groundwork
for all of these strategies now.

00:04:17.510 --> 00:04:21.770
We've read that Joe Biden and the Democratic
Party are also lawyering up.

00:04:21.770 --> 00:04:23.540
Are they going to be ready?

00:04:23.540 --> 00:04:26.980
And one of the difficulties is when you're
playing offense.

00:04:26.980 --> 00:04:31.350
You only need to come up with one strategy
the defense isn't prepared for and deploy

00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:32.350
it.

00:04:32.350 --> 00:04:36.040
When you're playing defense, you have to anticipate
every strategy in order to be prepared for

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:37.040
it.

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:38.590
And that's why this is so dangerous.

00:04:38.590 --> 00:04:41.500
What if it's simply not definitive?

00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:47.470
Come Election Day, Will Julian Zelizer, who
teaches history and public affairs at Princeton,

00:04:47.470 --> 00:04:51.440
says to the Atlantic that, quote, We are not
prepared for this at all.

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:55.530
We talk about it, some worry about it, and
we imagine what it would be.

00:04:55.530 --> 00:05:02.190
But few people have actual answers to what
happens if the machinery of democracy is used

00:05:02.190 --> 00:05:06.010
to prevent a legitimate resolution to the
election.

00:05:06.010 --> 00:05:09.780
Our democracy would be dead if Trump succeeds
at this.

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:13.610
If we fail, this is what happens.

00:05:13.610 --> 00:05:17.390
Republicans are making it clear they don't
win by democracy.

00:05:17.390 --> 00:05:21.020
They will win despite democracy, unable to
subvert democracy.

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:27.250
As David Frum said, if conservatives become
convinced that they cannot win democratically,

00:05:27.250 --> 00:05:31.250
they will abandon conservatism and they will
reject democracy.

00:05:31.250 --> 00:05:36.630
And by the way, it is not lost on me that
this is part of why they want to rush to replace

00:05:36.630 --> 00:05:38.470
Ruth Bader Ginsburg.

00:05:38.470 --> 00:05:40.770
That could end up being a factor.

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:42.720
We are really up against it here.

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:48.370
And it is just as appalling how Republicans
supporters, Republican voters are so entrenched

00:05:48.370 --> 00:05:54.710
in their team sport mentality that they were,
by and large, are standing by as Donald Trump

00:05:54.710 --> 00:05:56.230
develops these strategies.

00:05:56.230 --> 00:05:58.570
As long as they reject the Libs.

00:05:58.570 --> 00:05:59.990
Right, that's the point.

00:05:59.990 --> 00:06:02.570
They will accept blatant corruption.

00:06:02.570 --> 00:06:07.170
They will stand aside as democratic values,
not not capital D. Lowercase.

00:06:07.170 --> 00:06:12.720
The democratic values are dismantled and they
will let Trump do whatever the hell he wants.

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:13.720
We are up against it.

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:15.910
My friends, let me know what you think.

00:06:15.910 --> 00:07:22.200
I'm on Twitter

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:25.210
at David Pakman.

